      "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=1} & =3{q}^{′}(1)+4{r}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-4)+4(1) \\\\  & =-12+4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
